\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Scenario validation metrics (mean across 5 prompts, 100 permutations, $n=10$ responses, per-byte). We report several candidate scalars: unconditional surprise $a_1$, the asymptotic floor $a_n$, coherence $C$, our recommended score $D_{a_\infty } = C \times a_n$ (\textbf  {bold}), the excess entropy $E$ (Appendix~\ref {app:excess-entropy}), $C \times E$, and the coherence spread $\sigma _\ell $. $D_{a_\infty }$ correctly ranks multi-mode above one-mode and suppresses incoherent scenarios via $C$. Both $E$ and $C \times E$ go negative for the mixed scenario on GPT-2.}}{10}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:scenarios}{{1}{10}{Scenario validation metrics (mean across 5 prompts, 100 permutations, $n=10$ responses, per-byte). We report several candidate scalars: unconditional surprise $a_1$, the asymptotic floor $a_n$, coherence $C$, our recommended score $D_{a_\infty } = C \times a_n$ (\textbf {bold}), the excess entropy $E$ (Appendix~\ref {app:excess-entropy}), $C \times E$, and the coherence spread $\sigma _\ell $. $D_{a_\infty }$ correctly ranks multi-mode above one-mode and suppresses incoherent scenarios via $C$. Both $E$ and $C \times E$ go negative for the mixed scenario on GPT-2}{table.caption.10}{}}
