\newlabel{fig:mode-count}{{3}{12}{Mode count scaling on Qwen2.5-3B ($n=20$, 1000 draws). The $a_k$ curves fan out with increasing $m$: higher floors, slower convergence. All curves are exponential (no sigmoidal plateau), even at $m=10$, due to cross-mode learning (Section~\ref {sec:cross-mode-learning})}{figure.caption.13}{}}
